      "gguf": "loads at full context",
      "verdict": "GGUF"
    },
    "cost": "On Apple Silicon llama.cpp runs roughly 2.4x behind MLX because it does not use the neural accelerators.",
    "Nanbeige4.2-3B": {
      "lmstudio_mlx": "ValueError: Model type nanbeige not supported (mlx-llm 1.11.0)",
      "lmstudio_gguf": "llama-server exited before becoming healthy, exitCode=1 (llama.cpp 2.27.1)",
      "lms_runtime_update": "reports 'already up-to-date' - 2.27.1 is the newest offered",
      "upstream_llamacpp": "works (brew build 10210)",
      "verdict": "upstream llama.cpp only",
      "lesson": "It is not enough to choose between MLX and llama.cpp - the engine VERSION matters. LM Studio's bundled runtimes lagged the architecture support by weeks."
    },
    "_note_parallel": "LM Studio's PARALLEL setting multiplies KV cache. gpt-oss at 65536 context with PARALLEL 4 reached 18.75 GB wired (78 %) and made the desktop flicker; with --parallel 1 the same context peaked at 17.47 GB (73 %). For a single agent, one slot is enough."
  },
