    "conclusion": "Reducing the tool surface fixed gpt-oss (17 toolsets: failed; 2 toolsets: 22/22 in 2:28) but not Qwen3.5-9B, which failed either way. So tool width explains the 21B model's behaviour, not the 9B's. The same model solves this task 5/6 through a two-tool custom harness with terse schemas - Hermes' terminal+file toolsets still carry more functions and a much larger system prompt. For a local general-purpose agent on 24 GB the entry ticket is a 21B-class model at ~67 % memory, not the 39 % a 9B would have cost.",
    "caveat": "One run per configuration, not six. Enough to show the direction, not to quantify it. The gpt-oss contrast (fails at 17 toolsets, 22/22 at 2) is large enough that the direction is not in doubt; the Qwen3.5-9B result is a single failed run and should be read as such."
  }
